data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","item_id":"rs_0df0dc3b2715f59c016adf6a659f6c87d284f4ad4ad6fe33c8","output_index":0,"sequence_number":98,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Calculating divisible numbers**\n\nI need to derive a number based on certain conditions. I want to find how many numbers less than 10,000 are divisible by 3 and exactly one of 7 or 11. Using inclusion-exclusion, I'll count those divisible by 21 and 33, then adjust for those divisible by 231. After some calculations, I find the counts: 476 for 21, 303 for 33, and 43 for 231. Ultimately, the result is 693. I’ve confirmed it meets the conditions."}

